# Retro Arcade

A simple browser-based arcade website with classic mini-games built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

## Features

- Arcade menu with browser account login/signup
- Username + password account system using browser localStorage
- Profile stats saved per account
- Voice chat lobby with room code and direct invite flow
- Member list and better room controls

## Games Included

- Snake
- Pong
- Tic-Tac-Toe
- Call of Duty
- Voice Chat

## How to Run

Because this project is fully static, you can view it locally in a browser by opening `index.html` directly.

For a local web server, run:

```bash
python -m http.server 8000
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

## Account System

This project includes a local arcade account system using browser `localStorage` for a simple demo experience. Create an account from the home page, log in, and see your username reflected in the arcade and voice chat pages.

Note: this is a front-end demo, not a production-grade security system. For a real online app, use a backend service such as Firebase or Supabase Auth.

## Project Structure

- `index.html` — arcade home menu and account panel
- `login.html` — login form
- `signup.html` — account creation form
- `auth.js` — account storage and session logic
- `snake.html` — Snake game
- `pong.html` — Pong game
- `tictactoe.html` — Tic-Tac-Toe game
- `callofduty.html` — shooter-style game
- `voicechat.html` — browser microphone voice chat demo with room UI

## Notes

This project is designed as a lightweight front-end demo and does not require any framework or installation steps.






















































































































































































































